cdk: unpin the frozen grab cursor when the grab outlives the churn

The image cursorless grabs freeze on their window is meant for the
toggling grabs of a held key: the churn would otherwise flicker the
cursor between the theme's arrow and the window under the pointer at
the key repeat rate while the pointer sits still on, say, another
application's text box.  The first pointer movement under the grab
already unpins it, but the movement only reaches the grabbing client
while the pointer crosses its own windows, and a menu opened with a
single F10 press and no movement keeps the image pinned for as long
as the menu lasts: with the pointer parked on another client's text
box, the frozen text cursor then promises a click that the menu is
going to eat, the first click only dismisses the menu.

A grab that outlives the churn is not one of the toggling grabs
anymore.  Arm a timeout longer than any key repeat interval when the
image is frozen, re-armed by every toggle of the churn so it never
fires while the key repeats: when it fires with the grab still alive
on the same window, the unpin is the same NULL the pointer proxy
applies with the first movement, and the device swaps the frozen
image for the theme's default arrow, remembering it for the rest of
the grab.  Grabs that defined the arrow or an explicit cursor have no
frozen image and arm nothing.
